.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
A specialized search provider implementing binary-search-based probing\&. 

This provider assumes that the underlying \fITContainer\fP  is sorted according to the predicate or comparison logic used\&. It performs a midpoint probe to locate any matching element and then expands outward to collect all adjacent matches\&. This makes the provider efficient for clustered or repeated values in sorted sequences\&. 

.PP
\fBImportant:\fP This search provider is only valid for sorted containers\&. If the data is not sorted, use a linear search provider instead\&. 

.PP
\fBBehavior:\fP 
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRFind\fP returns the number of matching elements by probing the midpoint and expanding left/right until non-matching elements are encountered\&.   
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRWhere\fP returns all matching elements together with their indices\&.   
.IP "\(bu" 2
Matching is determined solely by the provided predicate or \fBISimpleCompare<T>\fP implementation\&.   
.PP

.PP
\fBTemplate Parameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIT\fP Element type stored in the container\&.
.br
\fITContainer\fP Container type implementing \fBIVector<T>\fP\&. Must provide indexed access and a stable element order\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBType Constraints\fP
.TP
\fITContainer\fP : \fIIVector<T>\fP
